{"kind":"assert","text":"To the checker: the record of a gate changes from f45b355a on. Hugh\napproved it on 14 November.\n\nFor each head filed after f45b355a, a gate leaves one log file in a\nnew directory under `~/play/artroom-evidence/`. The note's evidence\ntable cites the log by path and SHA-256. The head carries no\nmanifest, and the directory has no `SHA256SUMS` file and no\nread-only seal. No head owes a formal focused run, a power reading\nor a sleep record.\n\nYour check of the evidence becomes:\n\n1. The log exists at the path, and its SHA-256 equals the note's.\n2. Its first lines name the reviewed head and tree with 0 changed\n   files.\n3. Its last line says the gate passed.\n4. Each control that the note cites has its output in the same\n   directory.\n\nThe document-only follow-up rule of `docs/evidence-filing.md`\nstands. Your review of the change, its invariants and its\nwitnesses is as before.\n\n`docs/evidence-filing.md` still states the earlier record. Request\nGS-1 (b29bd21e) changes it. Until GS-1 lands, this act is the rule.\nThe combined head 256673de is the first head under it. Its focused\nrecord d5e93126 exists and stands.","body":{"to":"4817b532e7a1a118"}}